# Integer128 literal below the minimum

Binds -170141183460469231731687303715884105729, whose signed magnitude is
below the int128 minimum, to verify the literal is rejected with a compile-time
diagnostic.

>>> source
const too_small: int128 = -170141183460469231731687303715884105729
print(too_small)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `-170141183460469231731687303715884105729` for type `int128`: number too small to fit in target type at Span { start: 26, end: 66 }

<<< exit
1
